Package: mlxflow
Title: Model Building and Diagnostics Workflow for 'Monolix'
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Quentin", "Renou", email = "quentin.renou@amu-univ.fr", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Automates covariate model building for population pharmacokinetic
    models run with 'Monolix': stepwise backward elimination driven by
    likelihood ratio tests (through 'lixoftConnectors'), helpers around the
    'Monolix' COSSAC and SCM searches, readers for the 'Monolix' output files,
    diagnostic tables, plots and an 'Rmarkdown' report, and flowcharts of model
    building runs. This is an unofficial tool: it is not affiliated with, nor
    endorsed by, Lixoft or Simulations Plus.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/R-Quentin/mlxflow
BugReports: https://github.com/R-Quentin/mlxflow/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = FALSE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.1
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: dplyr, fs, ggplot2 (>= 3.5.0), ggraph, glue, igraph, kableExtra,
    knitr, patchwork, purrr, readr, rlang, rmarkdown, scales, stringr, tibble, tidyr
Suggests: lixoftConnectors, testthat (>= 3.2.0), withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
